# What `docker build` should not send to the daemon as build context (#600).
#
# The context is hashed on every build, so this is not only image size — it is
# how long the build takes to *start*, and how often the layer cache is missed
# for a file the image never wanted. `.git` alone is a couple of hundred
# megabytes here.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs what it needs explicitly (mix.exs, mix.lock, config,
# priv, lib, projects, assets, rel), so anything not listed there is dead
# weight. This file is the belt: excluding it keeps a stray local artifact —
# a dialyzer PLT under priv/, a node_modules, a built release — from riding
# into the image or busting a cached layer.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Build outputs and dependency trees. `mix deps.get` and `mix deps.compile` run
# inside the builder; a host copy is a different OTP/arch and would be worse
# than useless.
_build
_build_*
deps
cover
doc

# Dialyzer PLTs live under priv/, which the Dockerfile COPYs wholesale. They are
# large, host-specific, and of no use at runtime.
priv/plts

# Installed by `npm --prefix assets ci` in the builder.
assets/node_modules
e2e/node_modules
node_modules

# Test and local-development surface the image never runs.
test
e2e
.elixir_ls
.elixir-tools
.lexical
*.log

# Local environment and editor state.
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
.claude
.tool-versions.local
